      "value": {
        "status": "fail",
        "gate_id": "embodiment_contact_and_space",
        "reviewed_scales": [
          "native"
        ],
        "evidence": "The intended interaction targets do not all survive. The clerk pen visibly contacts a separate loose sheet behind the bound register, rather than the corresponding register entry required by the reviewed prompt. The left petitioner points to the left green parcel while the right petitioner points to the orange strip on the other bank. Administrator ruler/map contact itself is plausible, but the complete reviewed contact-target relationship fails; this is not a diagnosis of an unseen anatomical defect."
      },
      "source_role": "visual_review",
      "source_pointer": "/hard_gates/embodiment_contact_and_space",
      "source_sha256": "0f857e4747c8bec50ec4dbf8009d73b11ab0a41053bb3ac850712d7959400bad"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "status": "fail",
        "gate_id": "embodiment_visibility_and_projection",
        "reviewed_scales": [
          "native"
        ],
        "evidence": "The main face, hands, broad map and register are visible. However, the upper boundary/bridge connection on the large map is partly covered by the straightedge and administrator fingertip, so the entire required boundary route and every endpoint cannot be traced together with the matching register outline. The full planned comparison remains only partial at native scale. Nearby red lines and a visible lower bridge cannot pass the complete route gate."
      },
      "source_role": "visual_review",
      "source_pointer": "/hard_gates/embodiment_visibility_and_projection",
